@startuml Mobile Token Flow <<Seqence Diagram>>

actor User
participant MobileApplication 

participant nginx
participant oauth2Proxy
participant Keycloak

participant NodeJS
participant Redis
participant FHIR


== User Login Flow ==
User -> MobileApplication : Login request on login page
MobileApplication -> Keycloak : Redirect to auth endpoint (PKCE challenge)
Keycloak -> MobileApplication : Authorization code (Authz code Flow)
MobileApplication -> Keycloak : exchange code for tokens (with PKCE verifier)
Keycloak -> MobileApplication : Access token , Refresh token , ID token
MobileApplication -> MobileApplication : store tokens securely 
MobileApplication -> User : display main page

== User Action Requiring Data (API Call) ==
User -> MobileApplication : Action that needs Data
MobileApplication -> nginx : API call with token

alt Access token valid
nginx -> nginx : validate JWT (cached JWKS)
nginx -> NodeJS : forward request with access token
    alt resource available in cache
        NodeJS -> Redis : get resource from cache
        Redis -> NodeJS : resource
    else resource not in cache
        NodeJS -> FHIR : request resource with Access token
        FHIR -> NodeJS : resource
        NodeJS -> Redis : store resource in cache
        Redis -> NodeJS : ack
    end
    NodeJS -> nginx : response containing data
    nginx -> MobileApplication : response
    MobileApplication -> User : display data
else Access token expired
MobileApplication -> Keycloak : use refresh token to obtain new tokens
Keycloak -> MobileApplication : new Access token , new Refresh token , new ID token
MobileApplication -> nginx : API call with new Access token

end

== Logout Flow (Mobile — Per-session) ==
User -> MobileApplication : Tap "Sign out"
MobileApplication -> API (nginx) : POST /auth/logout { sessionId or accessToken }
nginx -> NodeJS : /auth/logout -> call RevocationService
RevocationService -> Redis : DEL oauth2_proxy:session:<id>
RevocationService -> Keycloak : POST /protocol/openid-connect/revoke (token) 
NodeJS -> MobileApplication : 200 OK
MobileApplication -> User : Signed out (this device)

== Logout Flow (Mobile — Global across mobile devices) ==
User -> MobileApplication : Tap "Sign out of all mobile devices"
MobileApplication -> API (nginx) : POST /auth/logout?scope=global
nginx -> NodeJS : /auth/logout -> call RevocationService { userId, deviceType=mobile }
RevocationService -> Redis : DEL keys matching userId and deviceType=mobile
RevocationService -> Keycloak Admin API : POST /admin/realms/{realm}/users/{id}/logout 
RevocationService -> NodeJS : 200 OK
NodeJS -> MobileApplication : redirect or success
MobileApplication -> User : all mobile sessions signed out
@enduml